 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 21147,
   "ANSWER": "<h3><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">System Calls Working</span></strong></span></span></span></h3>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The working of a system call involves a systematic transition of control from the user application to the kernel and back. This controlled interaction ensures security, resource protection, and process isolation.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">\ud83d\udd39</span> <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Step 1: Invocation by User Program</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">When a user program needs a service &mdash; such as reading a file, creating a process, or allocating memory &mdash; it makes a <strong>system call request</strong> via an API provided by standard libraries (e.g., <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">printf()</span></code> internally uses <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">write()</span></code> system call in UNIX-like systems).</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">\ud83d\udd39</span> <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Step 2: Trap Instruction Execution</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Instead of executing privileged instructions directly, the program executes a special <strong>trap instruction</strong>.</span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">This causes a <strong>software interrupt</strong>, transferring control from <strong>user mode to kernel mode</strong>.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The processor switches the mode to allow privileged operations.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">\ud83d\udd39</span> <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Step 3: System Call Handler Activation</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The OS identifies the requested system call using a <strong>system call number</strong> passed by the user program.</span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The <strong>system call interface (SCI)</strong> in the kernel maps this number to the corresponding system call handler.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The kernel validates parameters, checks permissions, and ensures the request complies with security policies.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">\ud83d\udd39</span> <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Step 4: Kernel Service Execution</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The kernel performs the requested operation, such as reading from a file, creating a process, or allocating memory.</span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">If successful, the kernel prepares the result.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">If an error occurs, an appropriate error code is generated.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">\ud83d\udd39</span> <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Step 5: Return to User Mode</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">After executing the system call, control is returned to the user program with the result or error code.</span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The processor switches back to <strong>user mode</strong>, restoring the execution state of the application.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Why Mode Switching is Crucial</span></strong></span></span></span></h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Protection:</strong> Prevents user programs from corrupting system resources.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Security:</strong> Ensures that only validated, authorized operations are executed.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Controlled Access:</strong> Enforces process isolation and access control policies.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Example of System Call Working (File Read Example)</span></strong></span></span></span></h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>User calls </strong><code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">read()</span></b></code><strong> function.</strong></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">read()</span></code> internally triggers a <strong>system call trap</strong>.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The kernel reads the file and retrieves data.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The data is returned to the user space.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Control returns to the next instruction in the user program.</span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"width:412px; height:331px\" /></span><b>&nbsp;</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Figure1: System call Implementation</span></b></span></span></span></p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO3",
    "PLO4"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><b>Explain the working of system calls in operating systems. How do they facilitate secure interaction between user applications and kernel services? Illustrate their operational flow with suitable explanation.</b></span></span></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 111,
   "TYPE": "lq",
   "key": 21147
  }
 ]
}